Third-party material
--------------------

- LineageOS (Apache-2.0)
  - device/fingerprint/: copied from LineageOS android_hardware_samsung (aidl/fingerprint), with its headers.
  - device/shims/libsensorndkbridge/: from LineageOS, with its headers.
  - device/extract-files.py, device/setup-makefiles.py and the makefile/blueprint skeletons follow the
    LineageOS device tree templates ("SPDX-FileCopyrightText: The LineageOS Project").

- Android Open Source Project / LineageOS (Apache-2.0)
  - reference/baseline/ and reference/system/: SELinux policy files produced by building AOSP system/sepolicy
    and LineageOS device/lineage/sepolicy. No Samsung content. tools/cil2te.py and the checks need them.
  - patches/frameworks/, patches/packages/apps/Settings/: changes to AOSP/LineageOS projects. They carry the
    license of the project they patch (Apache-2.0).

- PhhIms / ims-for-wisdom (GPL-2.0)
  - patches/packages/apps/PhhIms/: patches to https://github.com/xuanyayi/ims-for-wisdom (GPL-2.0, derived
    from krazey/ims and phhusson/ims). Patches 0001 and 0002 are upstream commits by krazey <admin@krazey.de>,
    with the original authorship kept in their headers. These patch files are GPL-2.0, not Apache-2.0.

- Samsung vendor SELinux policy (generated)
  - device/sepolicy/vendor/ is produced by tools/cil2te.py from the vendor policy (vendor_sepolicy.cil and
    contexts) of the stock A566BXXS6AYGE firmware. It is a mechanical conversion of Samsung's policy,
    included for interoperability so the stock vendor binaries run under SELinux; it is not covered by this
    repository's Apache-2.0 grant beyond what the author can grant. tools/cil2te.py regenerates it.

- Samsung / Exynos configuration text
  - device/rootdir/ (fstab, wifi.rc, recovery init scripts), device/configs/audio/ and parts of
    device/manifest.xml are modified versions of configuration files from the stock A566BXXS6AYGE firmware.
    Most Exynos device trees include files like these so that the stock vendor binaries can start. They are
    included only for interoperability. Files that would be verbatim stock copies (vendor/bin helper scripts,
    ramdisk configuration) are not in git: they are extracted like the blobs.

What this repository does NOT contain
-------------------------------------

No Samsung binaries and no stock firmware files:
- kernel, dtb, dtbo, kernel modules (.ko), vendor_boot ramdisk firmware, binaries and configuration: extracted locally from
  your own firmware with tools/extract_prebuilts.sh into the gitignored device/prebuilts/.
- vendor blobs: extracted locally with device/extract-files.py into vendor/samsung/essi (separate tree).
- reference/stock/ (the stock firmware's SELinux, init and VINTF files): filled locally by
  tools/populate_reference.sh. It is gitignored.

